hared":4,"play_caller":"Raheem Morris"},{"season":2022,"team":"NE","distance":0.4789,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2022,"team":"KC","distance":0.5155,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Steve Spagnuolo"}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Ravens are 4-3 through week 7 of the 2026 season and have outscored opponents 169 to 167. The offense has been carrying the team, ranking 8th in EPA per play while the defense sits 17th in EPA allowed. What sets them apart is the 2nd lowest early-down pass rate and the 2nd fewest defenders in the box in the league.","offense":"The Ravens offense has been well above average by EPA per play so far. Their run and pass mix has stayed close to what game situations call for. Tyler Huntley has run the passing game and leaned heavily on Zay Flowers, who has drawn 27% of the targets.","defense":"The Ravens defense has been about average by EPA allowed per play so far. Its strongest area has been explosive play rate allowed, where it ranks 10th, and its weakest has been takeaways per game, where it ranks 25th. Tavius Robinson leads the team with 3.5 sacks, and Mike Green has added 3 despite playing only 48% of the snaps. Schematically, they have the 2nd fewest defenders in the box in the league.","special":"The Ravens have been about average in how often they go for it on fourth down. Their kickers have made 80% of field goals, which is a little below average. On the roster side, they put an unusually large share of their salary cap into the quarterback, about 21% of the money on the books. Their defensive line was among the oldest in the league.","players":"Tyler Huntley has played nearly every snap at quarterback and thrown for 727 yards. Zay Flowers has been the clear top target with 27% of the looks and 608 receiving yards. Derrick Henry has handled most of the work in the backfield with 84% of the carries. On defense, Tavius Robinson leads the team with 3.5 sacks.","coaching":"Declan Doyle is calling the offense and Jesse Minter is calling the defense. Their offense looks most like the 2025 Bills under Joe Brady and the 2022 Titans. Their defense looks most like the 2023 Patriots and the 2022 Vikings.","trends":"The offense went from 12th in EPA per play in 2025 to 8th so far this season, a modest improvement. The defense moved from 20th in EPA allowed per play in 2025 to 17th so far this season, a modest improvement. The biggest change in approach was number of pass rushers, which went from 4.23 to 4.42.","notes":"The 2026 pages are built from data that nflverse updates every week, so they will keep changing until the season ends. Personnel, formations, coverage and pressure numbers are missing for now because that data is only released after the season."}}